# FIDVI Industries Cursor Rules

Read `FIDVI_DESIGN_GUIDE.md` before significant UI changes.

- Build a premium modern manufacturing/business website, not an IT/SaaS website.
- Use only the FIDVI black, warm-white, gold, charcoal and muted palette unless explicitly approved.
- Prefer premium serif display typography + clean sans-serif UI/body typography.
- Use large editorial typography, generous whitespace, thin borders and strong photography.
- Keep corner radii small; avoid excessive rounded cards and glassmorphism.
- Animate hierarchy, not everything. Prefer fade-up, image reveal, line reveal, subtle scale and arrow movement.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Prefer real FIDVI factory, machinery, process and product photography.
- Never invent certifications, clients, statistics, production capacity, specifications or capabilities.
- Reference images are not automatically FIDVI products unless confirmed.
- Reuse existing components before creating new ones.
- Prefer data-driven components over duplicated markup.
- Keep mobile behavior intentional and test desktop/mobile after major changes.
- Use semantic HTML, accessible forms, keyboard navigation, visible focus and proper alt text.
- Do not add unnecessary dependencies.
- Do not introduce unrelated colors, gradients, SaaS patterns or excessive animations.
- Do not redesign approved sections while implementing unrelated changes.
- Keep the final experience premium, restrained, editorial, manufacturing-focused and B2B-oriented.
